    "q-80650": {
      "dom_id": "step-q80650",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Find the values of $a$ and $b$, if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =a{y}^{3}{e}^{x-1}+3{x}^{2}{e}^{y-1}, \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & ={x}^{3}{e}^{y-1}+3b{y}^{2}{e}^{x-1}, \\\\ {f}_{x}(1,1) & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the mixed partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(a{y}^{3}{e}^{x-1}+3{x}^{2}{e}^{y-1}) \\\\  & =3a{y}^{2}{e}^{x-1}+3{x}^{2}{e}^{y-1} \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}{e}^{y-1}+3b{y}^{2}{e}^{x-1}) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}{e}^{y-1}+3b{y}^{2}{e}^{x-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the function and its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. Hence, we have the identity\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a{y}^{2}{e}^{x-1}+3{x}^{2}{e}^{y-1}=3{x}^{2}{e}^{y-1}+3b{y}^{2}{e}^{x-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of ${y}^{2}{e}^{x-1},$ respectively, we see that $a=b.$ \n\nSince ${f}_{x}(1,1)=4$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(1,1) & =4 \\\\ a(1)^{3}{e}^{0}+3(1)^{2}{e}^{0} & =4 \\\\ a+3 & =4 \\\\ a & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\nb=a=1.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-80650-a",
