    "q-133220": {
      "dom_id": "step-q133220",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Find the values of $a$ and $b$, if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =2ax{y}^{2}-4xy+15x, \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =b{x}^{2}y-2{x}^{2}-4y, \\\\ {f}_{y}(-1,-1) & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the mixed partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2ax{y}^{2}-4xy+15x) \\\\  & =4axy-4x-0 \\\\  & =4axy-4x \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(b{x}^{2}y-2{x}^{2}-4y) \\\\  & =2bxy-4x-0 \\\\  & =2bxy-4x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the function and its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. Hence, we have the identity\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4axy-4x=2bxy-4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $xy$, we see that $a=\\frac{b}{2}.$ \n\nNow, since ${f}_{y}(-1,-1)=-5$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(-1,-1) & =-5 \\\\ b(-1)^{2}(-1)-2(-1)^{2}-4(-1) & =-5 \\\\ -b-2+4 & =-5 \\\\ b & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na=\\frac{b}{2}=\\frac{7}{2}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
